 - 0 reg 1hr close - Default"}, "is_card_required": false, "is_grouped_calendar": false, "is_free_allowed": true, "is_no_tax": true, "sortable_index": 39250, "description": "## About\nExplore the life and influence of patriot Samuel Adams. The Man of the Revolution, Samuel Adams was also a man of contradictions. On this tour visit historic colonial sites as you learn about Samuel Adams' early business failures, his genius in the run-up to revolution, his descent into obscurity in the new republic, and why only his enemies called him \"Sam.\"\n\nAfter this special tour experience, raise a glass and show your support of Boston By Foot! Included in the price of your ticket is the choice between a souvenir Sam Adams tasting glass to take home with you, or a  drink at the Sam Adams Downtown Boston Taproom. (Over age 21 ID must be presented to the Taproom to redeem alcoholic beverages. Non-alcoholic soda options also available). BBF members receive a discounted ticket price.\n\nThis tour is presented in part thanks to the generous support of The Boston Beer Company.\n\n## Duration, Distance, Terrain\n1 hours\n.65 mile at a moderate pace, stopping at various sites along the tour\n\n## Meeting location:\nMeet your guide at the Samuel Adams Statue in front of Faneuil Hall.\n\nFinding Your Guide: All guides carry an 8×11 sign that says “Boston By Foot Walking Tours.”\n\nNearest MBTA Station: State (Orange and Blue Lines) \n\n## What to bring\nComfortable shoes, dress for the weather, water bottle", "description_text": "", "description_bullets": "", "seo_description": "", "location": "", "booking_notes": "", "cancellation_notes": "", "no_transportation_notes": "", "no_transportation_minutes": 15, "headline": "Explore the life and influence of patriot, Samuel Adams, then raise a glass at the Taproom after!", "short_description": "", "image_url": "", "image_cdn_url": "", "images": [{"cls": "Image", "uri": "/api/v1/companies/bostonbyfoot/items/523516/images/1132643/", "pk": 11326